-- title:
--   Two generators for an ordinary p-distinguished corner of H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain and $k$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is a field, with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\mathcal{O}\to k$ surjective; let $p$ be an odd prime with $k$ of characteristic $p$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M'$ and $p^2 \nmid M'$, and $H' \le (\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$ a subgroup containing every unit whose image under reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M'/p))^\times$ is $1$. Let $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$ have image in $\mathbb{Z}/(M'/p)$ equal to the class of $p$, and assume that the image of $d$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M'/p))^\times$, or its negative, lies in [`ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M' H' hpM`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L246), the image of $H'$ under that reduction. Let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers and suppose the endomorphisms [`CohCarrier.opFamily M' H' ↑S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) of $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_{H'}(M'),\mathcal{O})$, indexed by the generators [`CohCarrier.Gen M' ↑S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) ($T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M'$, $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M'$, and diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$) and built from transfer maps, commute pairwise. Let $\bar\theta : \mathrm{Gen} \to k$, and let $S'$ be an idempotent splitting of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra $\mathbb{T} = \mathcal{O}[\mathrm{op}]$ of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ generated by these operators: finitely many pairwise orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ summing to $1$, together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb{T}$ and satisfying $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j \iff i \ne j$. Fix an index $i_0'$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0'}\mathbb{T}e_{i_0'}$ to $k$ sending the corner of each generator's operator to $\bar\theta$ of that generator. Assume $\bar\theta(U_p) \ne 0$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional $k$-representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ trivial on the absolute Galois group of some number field, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$); assume that, viewed as an adic representation, it is ordinary at $p$, i.e. for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its nonunits there is a line $L$, spanned by a member of a basis, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and with the inertia subgroup acting trivially modulo $L$; assume further that $\bar\rho$ is $p$-distinguished, namely for some such $P$ and some $\sigma$ in its decomposition subgroup the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $(X-\alpha)(X-\beta)$ with $\alpha \ne \beta$ in $k$; and assume that for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M'$, every valuation subring $A$ with $\ell$ in its nonunits and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $A$, one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma) = \bar\theta(T_\ell)$. Then there exist $x, y$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0'} \cdot H^1$ such that the span, over the corner ring $e_{i_0'}\mathbb{T}e_{i_0'}$, of $\{x,y\}$ together with the set of all $a \cdot m$ with $a$ in the kernel of $\pi_k$ and $m$ in the corner submodule, is the whole corner submodule.
--
--   This is the two-generator bound of Wiles' multiplicity-one analysis for the ordinary, $p$-distinguished localisation of the weight-two cohomology of $\Gamma_{H'}(M')$ when $p$ exactly divides the level and the class of $p$ lies in $\pm H'$: the corner module needs only two generators modulo the maximal ideal $\ker \pi_k$. It is the step from which freeness of the corner submodule over the corner ring is deduced.
